# 001200-001299/20250204T051036Z_1273821282.wiki
zΔ⚡b|=25c6|+%3D%3D Usage %3D%3D%0AThe <code>diff</code> command is invoked from the command line, passing it the names of two files: <code>diff ''original'' ''new''</code>. The output of the command represents the changes required to transform the ''original'' file into the ''new'' file.%0A%0AIf ''original'' and ''new'' are directories, then {{Mono%7Cdiff}} will be run on each file that exists in both directories. An option, <code>%2Dr</code>, will recursively descend any matching subdirectories to compare files between directories.%0A%0AAny of the examples in the article use the following two files, ''original'' and ''new'':%0A{{Col%2Dbegin}}%0A{{Col%2Dbreak%7Cwidth%3D33%25}}%0A''original'':|=cf4|-1|=6beb|
